      <div type="document" n="o_szd.187">
      <pb n="1" facs="#surf_1"/>
      <p>
        <lb/>Any communication on the
        <lb/>subject of this letter should be
        <lb/>addressed to—
        <lb/>THE UNDER SECRETARY OF STATE,
        <lb/>ALIENS DEPARTMENT,
        <lb/>HOME OFFICE,
        <lb/>LONDON, S.W.I.
        <lb/>and the following number quoted:—
        <lb/>Z. 33.
      </p>
      <p>
        <lb/>                                     A 2 / 6   Z 33 1
      </p>
      <p>
        <lb/>                                     HOME OFFICE,
        <lb/>                                     WHITEHALL.
      </p>
      <p>
        <lb/>                                     29th June, 1934.
      </p>
      <p>
        <lb/>With reference to the application made on your
        <lb/>behalf by Mr. E. H. Carr; I am directed by the Secretary of
        <lb/>State to say that he does not desire to raise objection to
        <lb/>your prolonging your stay in this country provided that you
        <lb/>do not take employment.
      </p>
      <p>
        <lb/>                                     I am,
      </p>
      <p>
        <lb/>                                     Sir,
      </p>
      <p>
        <lb/>                                     Your obedient Servant,
      </p>
      <p>
        <lb/>                                     J. Hounes[?]
      </p>
      <p>
        <lb/>Mr. S. Zweig,
        <lb/>11, Portland Place,
        <lb/>W.1.
      </p>
      </div>
    </body>
